<title>USA: First Enterprise renegotiates credit line.</title>
<headline>First Enterprise renegotiates credit line.</headline>
<dateline>EVANSTON, Ill. 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Enterprise Financial Group Inc said Monday it has renegotiated its revolving credit facility, increasing the commitment to $85 million from $62 million.</p>
<p>The new arrangement also reduced the company's interest rate to prime plus 25 basis points with an option of 250 basis points over LIBOR from a previous prime plus one.</p>
<p>Chairman Michael Harrington said the specialty finance company's branch office network expanded to 33 at September, up from 29 at June 30.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
